                              "preview":  "Style: realistic with soft morning lighting. A close-up, handheld shot begins within a narrow florist shop at opening time. Soft morning light streams through the front glass, illuminating dust motes dancing in the air. The camera weaves intimately between colorful bouquets and the hands of a florist, a woman in her late 50s with kind eyes and graying hair pulled back into a bun. She wears a simple green apron over a floral blouse. The rich ambient audio includes the gentle crinkling of paper as she unwraps fresh flowers, the crisp snipping of scissors trimming stems, the sound of water filling a metal bucket, and a faint door chime in the background layered with distant street noise. The florist carefully trims a stem of a vibrant red rose, then gently unwraps a bundle of yellow tulips, their petals catching the light. She looks directly into the camera with a warm smile and says in a calm, gentle voice, “Can\u0027t beat the smell of fresh cut flowers.” The camera slowly pans to a row of flowers—a mix of lilies, carnations, and daisies—catching the soft morning light. As the shot lingers on the flowers, the front door opens with a gentle chime, revealing a glimpse of the outside world.",
